================================================================================
Relationship to Backspace
================================================================================

Rustspace is an unofficial, independent client and server written in Rust that
is compatible with Backspace.

  Backspace
  Copyright (c) 2026 Jannis Braun
  Official repository: https://github.com/TheZwiss/backspace
  License: AGPL-3.0-only

Parts of Rustspace are derived from Backspace: the network protocol, data model,
federation logic and server behaviour are ported from its TypeScript sources,
and some assets are taken from it unchanged (see below). Those parts remain
covered by Backspace's copyright and are used under the AGPL-3.0-only. In the
sense of section 5(a) of the AGPL, Rustspace is a modified version: it is a
rewrite in Rust with its own desktop client (egui), its own server
implementation and the changes recorded in this repository's git history.

Rustspace is not affiliated with, endorsed by or supported by Jannis Braun or
the Backspace project. Please report problems with Rustspace to the Rustspace
repository, not to Backspace.

"Backspace", the Backspace logo and the Backspace app icons are trademarks of
Jannis Braun. Rustspace does not use the Backspace logo or icons and does not
claim any rights to the Backspace name; it is mentioned only to describe
compatibility. The Rustspace "R" mark (packaging/brand/rustspace/,
packaging/linux/rustspace.*) is an original work of this project.

The commercial license offered for Backspace (LICENSE-COMMERCIAL.md in the
original repository) does not apply to Rustspace.

